AVER 0.0.14-alpha
\@COMM Example of a preinit.ares file, used to do some pre-init stuff.

\@COMM Write a really cool message, like your username and shell version!
\@WRITE "%USER : %ARES_VERSION "

\@COMM AEX still has no way of knowing time, so, we use BASH for it for now.
@bash -c 'printf "Session Started $(date)" > /tmp/000-ares-tmp'

\@COMM And print that data from the temporary file.
\@WRITE FROM /tmp/000-ares-tmp
AEND